Added MCP tools to edit the blocks of a page without resending all of them: `list_blocks` shows their ids and types, `add_blocks` inserts blocks after a given block or at a position, `update_block` changes one block, `remove_blocks` deletes blocks, and `set_blocks` replaces them while keeping the title and description blocks. They also work on blocks inside grids and other containers. Blocks can now be given as a list, each with an `@type`, to these tools and to `create_content` and `update_content`: ids and the layout are made for you, a string `href` becomes a list of links, and a block without `@type` is refused before anything is sent. The same steps are in the library as `operations.add_blocks`, `update_block`, `remove_blocks`, and `set_blocks`, with the helpers `blocks.normalize`, `tidy`, `locate`, `outline`, and `prepare`. @ericof
